  "prose": [
    {
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "Optical instruments often use triangular prisms made of glass or other transparent materials.\nThese prisms are among the most important components of instruments used to study the colors of light.\nThey are also used in telescopes, periscopes, and many other devices.",
      "id": null,
      "label": null,
      "printed_page": 185,
      "source_refs": [
        "p0195#6"
      ],
      "source_text": "在光学仪器中，常常要利用由玻璃或其它透明材料制成的三棱镜。这样的棱镜是研究光的颜色的仪器的最重要部件。它应用在望远镜、潜望镜和许多其它装置中。",
      "changes": [
        "language",
        "layout"
      ],
      "numeric_changes": [],
      "historical_entities": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "p",
      "text": "Figure 160 shows a cross-section of a glass prism taken perpendicular to its lateral edges.\nA ray passing through the prism is refracted twice, once at interface $OA$ and once at interface $OB$.\nThe angle $\\varphi$ between the two interfaces is called the **refracting angle of the prism**.\nThe ray's angle of deviation $\\theta$ depends on the prism's refracting angle $\\varphi$, the refractive index $n$ of its material, and the angle of incidence $\\alpha$.",
      "id": null,
      "label": null,
      "printed_page": 185,
      "source_refs": [
        "p0195#7",
        "p0195#10",
        "p0196#1"
      ],
      "source_text": "图160所示的是平面玻璃棱镜的与侧棱垂直的截面。光线在棱镜中折射两次：在交界面$OA$和$OB$上。两个交界面之间的角$\\varphi$叫做**棱镜的折射角**。光线的偏向角$\\theta$取决于棱镜的折射角$\\varphi$、棱镜材料的折射率$n$及入射角$\\alpha$。",
      "changes": [
        "language",
        "layout"
      ],
      "numeric_changes": [],
      "historical_entities": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "fig",
      "text": "",
      "id": "fig-160",
      "label": "Figure 160",
      "printed_page": 185,
      "source_refs": [
        "p0195#8"
      ],
      "source_text": "",
      "changes": [],
      "numeric_changes": [],
      "historical_entities": []
    },
    {
      "kind": "cap",
      "text": "Figure 160",
      "id": null,
      "label": "Figure 160",
